C COMPILER cc - EXACT SUPPORTED SUBSET (cc.c)

USAGE
  cc /tmp/foo.c     -> /tmp/foo.s
  as /tmp/foo.s     -> /tmp/a.out
  /tmp/a.out
Source <=1024 bytes. Output .s buffer <=4096 bytes, but as input
must be <=2048 bytes. No preprocessor, #include, headers or linker.

TOP LEVEL
  int main() { ... }              main required, must return int
  int sum(int a, int b) { ... }
  void helper(int *p) { ... }
  Up to 16 functions, up to 4 parameters each, supported parameter
  types int, int*, char*. Parameter names are identifiers <=19 chars.
  Function calls/recursion supported; fixed 256-byte local frame.
  Return values int; void functions may use return;.

LOCAL DECLARATIONS (inside a block/function)
  int n = 2;          char ch = 'A';
  int a[8];          char s[8] = "hi";
  int *p = &n;       char *q = &ch;
  Up to 16 variable names and local frame <=256 B per function.
  Arrays 1..64 elements, one dimension. Cannot declare pointer array.
  String initializer is supported for char arrays only.
  No global variables, struct, union, enum, typedef, const, static.

STATEMENTS
  assignment: n = n + 1;    a[0] = 3;    *p = 7;
  control: if (a < b) { ... } else { ... }
           while (n != 0) { ... }
  function call: helper(&n); return expr; or return; for void
  built-in: getpid(); read(fd,buffer,n); write(fd,buffer,n);
  write(1, "Hello\n", 6);  (special string-literal form)
  Expressions are small: + - * / %, unary + - & *, indexing,
  parentheses, constants, variables, sizeof(variable).
  Comparisons == != < <= > >= only in if/while conditions.
  Avoid &&, ||, !, +=, for, switch, ternary, casts.
  Scalar local int ++/-- is supported; see INCREMENT/DECREMENT below.

POINTERS AND NUMBERS
  Local int* and char* pointers, address-of local variable or
  array element, dereference and indexing. int* arithmetic scales
  by 4 bytes. No pointer-to-pointer, pointer return, pointer bounds
  checking or pointer-pointer subtraction. No arbitrary libc calls.
  Signed 32-bit constants accepted. Division/modulo implemented
  by repeated subtraction for nonnegative operands, not fast;
  division by zero returns 0 (do not rely on this).

ERRORS
  'unsupported C syntax or output too large' covers grammar,
  limits and assembly-buffer overflow. Split functions/source,
  use only supported syntax, and inspect generated foo.s.
  No runtime bounds checks: wrong addresses can corrupt memory.
  See /man/c-examples for full runnable snippets.

INCREMENT/DECREMENT: int scalar locals support i++, i--, ++i, --i.
Prefix yields the new value; postfix yields the old value. Pointer,
char, dereference and array-element increments are unsupported.
Generated .s files have a 2048-byte RAM-file limit independently of
1024-byte C source input and the 4096-byte internal code buffer.
An over-limit output is rejected before file creation; no partial .s.
